			<div class="content" id="post-content-2465029">
									

<p>Right, so, it's p good, just a few things I see right off the bat:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Grammar.</strong>
<ul>
<li><em>&quot;&#8230;via feeding tube, and a bedpan and/or relief tube&#8230;&quot;</em>
<ul>
<li>That should be a semicolon, not a comma, mate</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li><em>&quot;&#8230;regularly and before and after testing&#8230;&quot;</em>
<ul>
<li>That should read &quot;&#8230;regularly, both before and after testing&#8230;&quot;//</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>Other such small things</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li><strong>This:</strong> <em>&quot;&#8230;attach video game consoles or similar devices to televisions.&quot;</em>
<ul>
<li>It should not only read <em>&quot;&#8230;attach to&#8230;&quot;</em></li>
<li>But also, those could either be HDMI, VGA, or RGB cables. Please clarify.</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li>Not sure what that communique at the bottom is, but it leaves absolutely no context.</li>
</ul>
<p>Those are the only problems I see as of right now; however, there may be more.</p>

