<p>oddly enough, that bit is actually one of the more plausible elements here- the whole &quot;stimulating the pleasure centers&quot; thing is actually a real thing. Really effective way of getting rats to push a button until they starve. During early medical trials of electrical brain stimulation for treating epilepsy and mental illness, there were also a couple unfortunate incidents involving misplaced electrodes demonstrating that people are only slightly more resistant to the same &quot;<a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wirehead_%28science_fiction%29">Wirehead</a>&quot; effect.</p>

